<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-all</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:08:01Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-all" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-all" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Nepal's leader says his country is paying the price of climate change</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eda68425107d7d632d5e76b93195a06261d41c09f48816206161f89e84a0eea3</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T04:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nepal-s-leader-says-his-country-is-paying-the-price-of-climate-change/a-79421807--a05a6077a529.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nepal-s-leader-says-his-country-is-paying-the-price-of-climate-change/a-79421807?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nepalese Prime Minister Balendra Shah called the devastating Nepal-Tibet floods a "warning to the world" — and questioned if the world had "really heard that warning."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Jürgen Klopp starts Germany job with shaky Netherlands draw</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ffff30ea64415990be67f46843361dc3355000d1215bf9f4e7e433e5f6a0fffd</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T22:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/j_rgen-klopp-starts-germany-job-with-shaky-netherlands-draw/a-79420143--fa995d928e4d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/jürgen-klopp-starts-germany-job-with-shaky-netherlands-draw/a-79420143?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A late Netherlands goal denied Jürgen Klopp a win in his first match as Germany coach. The former Liverpool and Borussia Dortmund boss has big ambitions, but the game showed he's going to need more time to achieve them.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>UNGA Day 3: Netanyahu defends Israel as delegates walk out</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ddc824197aeee97ed158a74cf05af89e2ae9d742694f3be3eb6a1025b20a58b8</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:58Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T19:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/unga-day-3-netanyahu-defends-israel-as-delegates-walk-out/live-79366211--ad1d3eff9b7d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/unga-day-3-netanyahu-defends-israel-as-delegates-walk-out/live-79366211?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu called accusing Israel of genocide in Gaza the "greatest lie of the century." Many delegates walked out for his General Assembly speech. Mahmoud Abbas also spoke via video.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Three-way battle for power in world chess: Who will be elected FIDE president in Samarkand?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:00b1c0565d047241e68794c4dd6cf9c104e42672929b33560104f20087b18f5a</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301--bc60333e85fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The era of Russian presidents is coming to an end at the World Chess Federation (FIDE). Two Germans and one Kazakh are up for election. Among the issues at play are money, Kremlin influence, and unanswered questions.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia's military says it killed hundreds of TPLF rebels</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1794a4181c208ce3cf35aa7ad3bf3a83ffdf62ff1ba7d3b1dc4d9dfa453fd12e</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-s-military-says-it-killed-hundreds-of-tplf-rebels/a-79419173--d10c751c44c1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-s-military-says-it-killed-hundreds-of-tplf-rebels/a-79419173?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The TPLF fought against against the Ethiopian military from 2020 to 2022 in a conflict that saw hundreds of thousands of civilians killed. A resumption of fighting has sparked fears of another brutal war.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>After several difficult years, economists now expect German economy to grow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:86552b8edd8f6a3242b3c14abf719449139599bcc24774ea84a01608cf9385bd</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T17:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/after-several-difficult-years-economists-now-expect-german-economy-to-grow/a-79418591--9a99d252976e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/after-several-difficult-years-economists-now-expect-german-economy-to-grow/a-79418591?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's economy is growing again, but recovery remains on shaky ground. High government spending is keeping the economy afloat, while energy prices, a shortage of skilled workers and debt continue to weigh on it.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>CNN, MS NOW, Politico regain access to White House</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d5f8064a0f10e172c7d32e2dbeec348248589d78975a16bef7d82188652ebd8d</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T16:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cnn-ms-now-politico-regain-access-to-white-house/a-79405693--d2a4fb75d5c1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cnn-ms-now-politico-regain-access-to-white-house/a-79405693?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A federal judge has ordered President Trump to restore White House access to CNN, MS NOW and Politico after he banned the media outlets from the premises. Hours later, the media announced they had been granted access.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Houthi advances in Yemen drive displacement, deepen humanitarian crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f91e8371c2a3a6cd3007fb7dfa8e10907904eb934151f540d7747dd70d04c2e</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T16:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/houthi-advances-in-yemen-drive-displacement-deepen-humanitarian-crisis/a-79414280--b87656e50311.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/houthi-advances-in-yemen-drive-displacement-deepen-humanitarian-crisis/a-79414280?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With more than 132,000 people already displaced by the latest fighting and Houthi territorial gains, Yemen is on the brink of slipping back into a full-fledged humanitarian emergency. DW spoke with people on the ground.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria, US agree to boost mining investment on sidelines of UN General Assembly</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7cae359324721c46aaa6edfca7a077565f664f7f4c14366417502e1b1f46edd7</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T15:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-us-agree-to-boost-mining-investment-on-sidelines-of-un-general-assembly/a-79417444--0b49b11ac5c8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-us-agree-to-boost-mining-investment-on-sidelines-of-un-general-assembly/a-79417444?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">On the sidelines of the UN General Assembly, Nigeria and the US inked a new mining deal. Nigeria is home to deposits of lithium, gold, tin, gemstones, iron ore and phosphate.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Extremist parties are thriving ― and that scares people</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:314f2bc6c20a1a569abb5bcc55c730ebbbc254d2dabdf39241d61b1139638330</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T14:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/extremist-parties-are-thriving-_-and-that-scares-people/a-79410960--03e11a3885b2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/extremist-parties-are-thriving-―-and-that-scares-people/a-79410960?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Far-right and far-left parties are celebrating success after success, leaving moderate politicians in the dust and worrying many Germans. Political psychology helps us understand what's behind growing polarization.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>How renewed fighting in Tigray could spread across the Horn of Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2432c9014eac57c87708b041c4933502a8230fc196b1701c50d682861d8d67c8</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T13:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-renewed-fighting-in-tigray-could-spread-across-the-horn-of-africa/a-79410333--a598375bf2c9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-renewed-fighting-in-tigray-could-spread-across-the-horn-of-africa/a-79410333?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The fresh hostilities in Ethiopia's Tigray region come after months of growing animosity between rebel forces and the federal government. Horn of Africa expert Martin Plaut warns of possible regional spillover.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Donald Trump hosts Xi Jinping for state dinner with tech titans. Follow live.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0bf5e3a036c6f758ddc087641106474dce765f3a060a1fd85bce9f15fbc062a4</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:08:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T13:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/donald-trump-hosts-xi-jinping-for-state-dinner-with-tech-titans-follow-live/live-79404511--d8b5960a2742.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/donald-trump-hosts-xi-jinping-for-state-dinner-with-tech-titans-follow-live/live-79404511?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump rolled out the red carpet for Chinese leader Xi Jinping, with the two having toasted each other at a lavish state dinner after their summit meeting. America's top tech bosses were also present at the dinner.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU to condemn war in Ukraine at G20 even if Putin attends</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:228a83fcc0f025bd7201adb9fd3472eb6abe2f58b8d5f71b2c88669f980ab53f</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T13:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-to-condemn-war-in-ukraine-at-g20-even-if-putin-attends/a-79413317--3809a660b511.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-to-condemn-war-in-ukraine-at-g20-even-if-putin-attends/a-79413317?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russian President Vladimir Putin has been invited to the G20 summit in Miami by the United States. Multiple members of the group have called for Moscow's exclusion over its invasion of Ukraine.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>AI systems shifted their answers toward both left- and right-leaning users in a study. Could sycophantic chatbots deepen political divides?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8347d346899a7978b591529abce9ccdeb52c8f1b59047fe1a0a1040061f549c9</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T13:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ai-systems-shifted-their-answers-toward-both-left-and-right-leaning-users-in-a-study-could-sycophant/a-79377894--6126140be276.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ai-systems-shifted-their-answers-toward-both-left-and-right-leaning-users-in-a-study-could-sycophantic-chatbots-deepen-political-divides/a-79377894?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A study shows chatbots mirror users' politics, part of a broader tendency known as AI sycophancy. Researchers fear this could deepen polarization.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Berlin officially withdraws Olympics bid</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d008a17c2cef94230b5c3d50bef1fdc69028ba3b6d131eb4cdc7f2e3d3a7233d</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T12:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-berlin-officially-withdraws-olympics-bid/live-79406294--30622a12ce08.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-berlin-officially-withdraws-olympics-bid/live-79406294?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Berlin's decision to withdraw its Olympic bid means that only Munich and the western Rhine/Ruhr region are left in the running as potential Olympic hosts. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Czech PM Andrej Babis reiterates importance of NATO for his country but rejects calls to increase defense spending</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6c5344418dff728561819a3629f6a4412b0bb126844f9e085611cf02f06cab03</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T12:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/czech-pm-andrej-babis-reiterates-importance-of-nato-for-his-country-but-rejects-calls-to-increase-de/a-79411066--415ccd460a40.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/czech-pm-andrej-babis-reiterates-importance-of-nato-for-his-country-but-rejects-calls-to-increase-defense-spending/a-79411066?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US and NATO want Czechia to spend more on defense. Czech Prime Minister Andrej Babis says Prague cannot afford faster increases, despite growing warnings about the threat from Russia.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>'Pope fever' takes hold as Pope Leo visits France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3359e02711e4e0535bba4d464a73193627c8995b4ef192e46fe25046c347f7f7</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T12:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pope-fever-takes-hold-as-pope-leo-visits-france/a-79401291--1edb64ca4ad9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pope-fever-takes-hold-as-pope-leo-visits-france/a-79401291?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV is expected to draw huge crowds during his visit to France. As part of his trip, he's also set to address Europe's future and some of the challenges ahead.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU finally clinching trade deals with Southeast Asian states</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:efcfee522074a46eb4dc1492188d2ea41fbb0e4ace5b312f10be0c8cdf275e73</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T11:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-finally-clinching-trade-deals-with-southeast-asian-states/a-79388278--8c0030248950.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-finally-clinching-trade-deals-with-southeast-asian-states/a-79388278?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After years of arduous negotiations, the EU is closing on a string of bilateral trade deals with countries in Southeast Asia. And yet, a bloc-to-bloc agreement between the EU and ASEAN remains a distant prospect.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Tensions between India and Bangladesh are in focus after Dhaka skipped the BRICS summit in Delhi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e9cca3761845be2b1a2de5e394b7ed011129abdbf1ef012c309eea4e249f44f6</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T11:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tensions-between-india-and-bangladesh-are-in-focus-after-dhaka-skipped-the-brics-summit-in-delhi/a-79410667--fb62a16b78a2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tensions-between-india-and-bangladesh-are-in-focus-after-dhaka-skipped-the-brics-summit-in-delhi/a-79410667?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bangladesh's absence from the BRICS summit in New Delhi has raised fresh questions about strained ties. Ousted PM Sheikh Hasina's exile in India remains a major obstacle to normalizing relations.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Cockroach party demands Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar's resignation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b22fb9c73201f53fb7d8c72938c9b3701ba919086e5c950699f800613f665d5b</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T11:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-cockroach-party-demands-election-commissioner-gyanesh-kumar-s-resignation/live-79405879--428579042cfb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-cockroach-party-demands-election-commissioner-gyanesh-kumar-s-resignation/live-79405879?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">CJP's Abhijeet Dipke has alleged that the removal of more than 130 million names from draft electoral rolls is designed to benefit the BJP and weaken opposition parties. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Could a Left Party government in Berlin expropriate large real estate companies?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7e4363b570f06c04bb0f6c6d48c2cee8d5e52f9b510a6ca22bf99349793c3885</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T14:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/could-a-left-party-government-in-berlin-expropriate-large-real-estate-companies/a-79399683--c9f46d7db0c4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/could-a-left-party-government-in-berlin-expropriate-large-real-estate-companies/a-79399683?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The socialist Left Party won the Berlin election partly on the promise to implement the city's 2021 expropriation referendum as a way to solve the city's rent crisis. But can it really happen?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>China's 13-year-old swimming star raises questions on child athletes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ffc2d573cd23aae2b3fb90b8a2cf3d015b9b31afdc35ed4705bbad408af5722</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T14:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-s-13-year-old-swimming-star-raises-questions-on-child-athletes/a-79394183--95db71a677f9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-s-13-year-old-swimming-star-raises-questions-on-child-athletes/a-79394183?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Three gold medals and three Asian Games records have catapulted China's Yu Zidi, 13, into the sporting spotlight. She is far from the first teen prodigy, but should teens be competing at elite level?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Slovakia: PM Robert Fico's NATO Article 5 remarks spark criticism and raise questions about his country's NATO commitment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:14eb074e8514b5900c319b624ebaf975ac7f754663e93424c37d6f8d888de37d</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T13:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/slovakia-pm-robert-fico-s-nato-article-5-remarks-spark-criticism-and-raise-questions-about-his-count/a-79387050--e3e0d18cd9d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/slovakia-pm-robert-fico-s-nato-article-5-remarks-spark-criticism-and-raise-questions-about-his-country-s-nato-commitment/a-79387050?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Slovak Prime Minister Robert Fico says he fears war and will do everything he can to keep his country out of one. Critics say his remarks risk weakening NATO, the alliance that was designed to prevent such a war.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's oldest party, the center-left SPD, is in a difficult position following its success in the Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania state election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:533af5c251cf2ae3fa9c661096597cff953937c0114d3f6c519d5f565af42e67</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T13:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-oldest-party-the-center-left-spd-is-in-a-difficult-position-following-its-success-in-the-m/a-79376827--2a4f42a68594.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-oldest-party-the-center-left-spd-is-in-a-difficult-position-following-its-success-in-the-mecklenburg-western-pomerania-state-election/a-79376827?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chancellor Friedrich Merz (CDU) has vowed to press ahead with controversial reforms, but resistance is mounting within his coalition partner, the SPD. How much dissent can a governing coalition tolerate?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Munich and Cologne-Rhine-Ruhr – Germany's two remaining Olympic candidates</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:76ecd5a3d348cee428cb37f967f2d7af515b19a94a11dfbe96106ac438b199d3</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T11:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/munich-and-cologne-rhine-ruhr-germany-s-two-remaining-olympic-candidates/a-79386915--bae1fd64c3bb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/munich-and-cologne-rhine-ruhr-germany-s-two-remaining-olympic-candidates/a-79386915?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Munich or the Cologne-Rhine-Ruhr region? Germany aims to host the Olympic Games again. Just two candidates are left after Berlin pulled out at the last minute.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>El Nino explained: How the weather pattern affects hurricanes and tropical storms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0be905f915569229fc7902d1840c4c8a22183180b3b6ced717a116ad72fa971a</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T09:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/el-nino-explained-how-the-weather-pattern-affects-hurricanes-and-tropical-storms/a-79382511--be7cc5c8c0e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/el-nino-explained-how-the-weather-pattern-affects-hurricanes-and-tropical-storms/a-79382511?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From drought to major floods and extreme heat, El Nino will have a huge impact on the world's weather. In the Atlantic, it could mean a season without hurricanes.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>China's new travel rules unsettle tech giants and talent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:46a1f4b42d3e1635c1788b29121cd5ed9d0703f617a24f98cfba14595cca030c</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T08:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-s-new-travel-rules-unsettle-tech-giants-and-talent/a-79319937--16d904ca4025.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-s-new-travel-rules-unsettle-tech-giants-and-talent/a-79319937?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Beijing is locking the gates to stop expertise and capital in strategic industries from fleeing. The country accused of industrial-scale intellectual property theft now fears the West will take its own.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Famine threatens the Ukrainian town of Oleshky in the southern Kherson region as Russia delays creating a humanitarian evacuation corridor</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c485b406f9ce217f381150510ccafcdcdc54adea208ef45cf6fddee48387ad42</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T08:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/famine-threatens-the-ukrainian-town-of-oleshky-in-the-southern-kherson-region-as-russia-delays-creat/a-79380887--1d1c80d27c3d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/famine-threatens-the-ukrainian-town-of-oleshky-in-the-southern-kherson-region-as-russia-delays-creating-a-humanitarian-evacuation-corridor/a-79380887?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Food supplies to the town of Oleshky, in the occupied part of the southern Kherson region, have been cut off since May. Efforts by Kyiv to negotiate the evacuation of civilians with Moscow have been largely unsuccessful.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Call to scrap once-a-day gas price rises</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:597d108f747c691e0a145f5a6fd16a2ed1e6a26d3b51f475f08d66089c0c3948</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T07:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-call-to-scrap-once-a-day-gas-price-rises/live-79382523--75528f1f86f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-call-to-scrap-once-a-day-gas-price-rises/live-79382523?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The ADAC motoring association says a once-a-day rule on gas price changes has failed to help drivers' wallets. Entry-level jobs are becoming scarcer, making things hard for those entering the job market. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Military aircraft crashes near US air base in Spangdahlem, Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e166ddaeb1ceb063fdd5d12a28bc0883321ac75a93fed5da8e8d360a2160e102</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T14:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/military-aircraft-crashes-near-us-air-base-in-spangdahlem-germany/a-79376025--82e638c408d1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/military-aircraft-crashes-near-us-air-base-in-spangdahlem-germany/a-79376025?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The F-16 pilot was able to safely eject from the plane and was taken to receive medical care. The incident occurred near Spangdahlem Air Base in the German state of Rhineland-Palatinate.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Young Berliners vote overwhelmingly for socialist Left  Party</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ce7d6c0d5476cc03bfcd65e54f7bcf728bcf1f1d24285ba1eedbee32785188e8</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T14:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/young-berliners-vote-overwhelmingly-for-socialist-left-party/a-79375167--9c7d9060df7e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/young-berliners-vote-overwhelmingly-for-socialist-left-party/a-79375167?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Berlin's young voters overwhelmingly supported the victorious socialist Left Party. Are the young more radical? Or are the election results just a reflection of current German politics?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Living in the shadow of LA's hidden oil wells</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b87d0a56546acf2d8c949c3b7b2fb1b6104c28f77ac70f22006ab9dfc1182a03</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:06:51Z</